{{!
    @template tool_lp/competency_plan_navigation

    Jump to another competency of the same learning plan, overridden by Dimensions.

    Mirrors tool_lp/competency_plan_navigation of Moodle 5.3 (2026100500),
    admin/tool/lp/templates/competency_plan_navigation.mustache. Re-diff it against that file on every
    core upgrade.

    Kept from core, because tool_lp/competency_plan_navigation and core/form-autocomplete read them:
    the select's id competency-nav-<uniqid>, its label, its form-select class, every option with its
    value and selected state, and the JavaScript itself. The competency shortname keeps core's triple
    stash and the idnumber its double stash.
    Changed: the panel is the theme's (dim-comp-nav) in place of core's bordered box; core's float
    from sm up stays.
    The JavaScript is core's statement for statement, with the constructor's parameter capitalised
    (Nav) and long lines wrapped: core's copy has no example context and was never linted.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * userid, competencyid, planid, baseurl - read by the JavaScript
    * hascompetencies - boolean
    * competencies - array of id, shortname, idnumber, selected

    Example context (json):
    {
        "userid": 3,
        "competencyid": 1,
        "planid": 4,
        "baseurl": "https://example.com/admin/tool/lp/user_competency_in_plan.php",
        "hascompetencies": true,
        "competencies": [
            {"id": 1, "shortname": "Communicate clearly", "idnumber": "COMM-1", "selected": true},
            {"id": 3, "shortname": "Listen actively", "idnumber": "COMM-2", "selected": false}
        ]
    }
}}
<div class="dim-comp-nav float-sm-end">
{{#hascompetencies}}
<span class="dim-comp-nav__group">
<label for="competency-nav-{{uniqid}}" class="accesshide">{{#str}}jumptocompetency, tool_lp{{/str}}</label>
<select class="form-select" id="competency-nav-{{uniqid}}">
{{#competencies}}
<option value="{{id}}" {{#selected}}selected="selected"{{/selected}}>{{{shortname}}} {{idnumber}}</option>
{{/competencies}}
</select>
</span>
{{/hascompetencies}}
</div>
{{#js}}
require(['core/form-autocomplete', 'tool_lp/competency_plan_navigation'], function(autocomplete, Nav) {
    (new Nav('#competency-nav-{{uniqid}}', '{{baseurl}}', {{userid}}, {{competencyid}}, {{planid}}));
{{#hascompetencies}}
    autocomplete.enhance('#competency-nav-{{uniqid}}', false, false, {{# quote }}{{# str }}jumptocompetency, tool_lp{{/ str }}{{/ quote }});
{{/hascompetencies}}

});
{{/js}}
